USA."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136367"} "Ryan Murphy"] " started it out for the USA with a world record of 51.85 on the opening backstroke leg. However, Great Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/134063"} "Adam Peaty"] " blasted the breaststroke leg in 56.69 to give Britain the lead after the second leg. Unfortunately for the field, Phelps was the third US swimmer, and his butterfly leg of 50.33 bade farewell to the Olympics, and to the other teams in the race. It was left for Nathan Adrian to bring it home for the Americans as they won gold by 1.29 seconds. Britain held on for silver in a national record 3:29.24, while Australia took bronze. For Phelps this was his 23rd gold medal and 28th Olympic medal, all records that could stand forever."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:31.83 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:27.95 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/115617"} "Nathan Adrian"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136353"} "Caeleb Dressel"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136357"} "Cody Miller"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136358"} "David Plummer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136365"} "Kevin Cordes"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136367"} "Ryan Murphy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136369"} "Tom Shields"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws